 ### [Spherical Harmonics Representation](10084-spherical-harmonics-representation.md)
-Spherical Harmonics (SH) is a mathematical basis used in 3D Gaussian Splatting to represent the view-dependent color of each Gaussian primitive [G]. It adds view-dependent color representation to Gaussians, capturing appearance variations that a single static RGB value cannot represent [G]. An analytical Jacobian propagates gradients from SH to camera poses during optimization, though this may marginally worsen trajectory estimates if SH incorrectly models non-view-dependent effects caused by camera motion [G].
