 ### [7D Gaussian Splatting](11462-7d-gaussian-splatting.md)
-7D Gaussian Splatting (7DGS) is a unified framework for the real-time rendering of dynamic scenes with complex view-dependent effects, representing scene elements as seven-dimensional Gaussians spanning spatial position (3D), time (1D), and viewing direction (3D) [G]. It solves the problem of simultaneously modeling spatial geometry, temporal dynamics, and view-dependent appearance (such as scattering and anisotropic reflections) in dynamic scenes, a challenge that prior methods like 4DGS and 6DGS addressed in isolation [G]. Unlike its siblings, 7DGS jointly models all three dimensions in a single coherent framework, using a conditional slicing mechanism to transform 7D Gaussians into time- and view-conditioned 3D Gaussians compatible with existing 3DGS rendering pipelines [G].
